Description: Estimates two-class mixture graded response models for rating
    scales that mix positively and negatively worded items. Respondents in an
    inconsistent class may misread each reverse-worded item with an
    item-specific probability, which can be fixed to one (the ordinal analogue
    of the constrained factor mixture model of Steinmann, Strietholt, and
    Braeken, 2022 <doi:10.1037/met0000392>), estimated freely, or explained by
    item characteristics. Class membership is regressed on person covariates
    such as reading proficiency in the same estimation step, with support for
    plausible values, sampling weights, and cluster-robust standard errors.
    Estimation is by marginal maximum likelihood with an EM algorithm.
    Tools for model comparison, parametric bootstrap likelihood-ratio tests,
    person-level classification, and simulation are included.
